<%= generated_header("Dovecot passwd-file — used as BOTH passdb and userdb.") -%>
#
# Format, and the reason this file is validated character by character:
#
#   user:password:uid:gid:gecos:home:shell:extra_fields
#
# The separator is ":", not newline. A ":" smuggled into a local part does not
# corrupt one field, it SHIFTS every field after it — and two positions along is
# the numeric uid. MailConfig rejects ":", "=", ",", whitespace and "#" in every
# field for exactly this reason.
#
# uid/gid are popuser:popuser (<%= MailConfig::VMAIL_UID %>:<%= MailConfig::VMAIL_GID %>), written from constants and never from a
# column: which uid Dovecot reads and writes files as is not a per-mailbox
# decision, and the 143 MB already on disk is owned by exactly this pair.
#
# EVERY active mailbox on an active domain has a line here, credential or not,
# because this file is the userdb as well as the passdb: Postfix delivers over
# LMTP, Dovecot answers a userdb miss with a permanent 5.1.1, and Postfix has
# already accepted the message by then — a missing line is a BOUNCE, not a
# login failure.
#
# A mailbox with no credential yet gets <%= MailConfig::NO_PASSWORD %> in the password field. No
# password can produce that, so it fails closed; an EMPTY field is deliberately
# not used, because empty is a credential question and this is not. All nine
# accounts start without a credential — six shared one password and one was used
# to relay ~12k phishing messages, so the migration is a reset, not a copy.
#
# Install 0640 root:dovecot. It holds password digests.
<% if credential_less_rows.any? -%>
#
# <%= credential_less_rows.size %> of the accounts below cannot authenticate until someone resets them:
<% credential_less_rows.each do |row| -%>
#   <%= row[:address] %>
<% end -%>
<% end -%>
<% passwd_rows.each do |row| -%>
<%= row[:address] %>:<%= row[:password] %>:<%= MailConfig::VMAIL_UID %>:<%= MailConfig::VMAIL_GID %>::<%= row[:home] %>::<%= row[:extra].join(" ") %>
<% end -%>
<% if passwd_rows.empty? -%>
# (no active mailbox on any active domain)
<% end -%>
